cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AnalysisXMD: A browser-based dashboard for protein–ligand molecular dynamics analysis"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Kevin Anthony"
    family-names: "Oré Maldonado"
    email: k.ormaldonado@uandresbello.edu
    affiliation: "Computational Chemistry Research Group, Universidad Andrés Bello (UNAB), Chile"
abstract: >-
  AnalysisXMD is a lightweight, single-file web dashboard for the analysis and
  visualization of molecular dynamics simulations of protein–ligand systems.
  It reads native GROMACS and AMBER (cpptraj) output and provides RMSD, RMSF,
  PCA, distance, hydrogen-bond, multi-replica, and RMSD density (KDE) analyses,
  an interactive trajectory viewer with VMD-style playback, and
  publication-quality figure export (300–600 DPI PNG and editable SVG).
keywords:
  - molecular dynamics
  - protein-ligand
  - GROMACS
  - AMBER
  - NAMD
  - cpptraj
  - RMSD
  - RMSF
  - hydrogen bonds
  - computational chemistry
  - data visualization
